  "description": "Secluded corner two bedroom apartment in a mature leafy setting.\n\nNo. 158 Bushy Park is an immaculately presented two bedroom ground floor apartment, set within one of South Dublin's most sought after and mature residential developments. \n\nBoth bedrooms are spacious doubles, with the main bedroom further enhanced by a well-appointed ensuite. The layout is both practical and elegant, offering a sense of space and flow that works effortlessly for modern living. A standout feature of the apartment is the large private terrace, which overlooks the beautifully landscaped communal grounds and provides a peaceful outdoor retreat — ideal for morning coffee, entertaining, or simply enjoying the tranquil surroundings.\n\nBuilt by the highly regarded Sheelin McSharry in the former estate lands associated with Our Lady's secondary school. These historic grounds, once part of a grand demesne dating back to the early 18th century, lend a sense of heritage and established elegance to the development, blending seamlessly with the contemporary homes now thoughtfully positioned within them.\n\nThis refined home combines generous proportions, excellent design, and an enviable setting, making it ideally suited to downsizers seeking ease and comfort, first-time buyers stepping onto the property ladder, and investors seeking quality and long-term appeal\n\nThe location is idyllic and leafy yet extremely convenient.\n\nSet within mature, parklike grounds, the development enjoys a unique sense of history and character while being exceptionally convenient.\n\nThe location is exceptional, positioned between the vibrant villages of Terenure and Templeogue, both just a short stroll away and offering an excellent array of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and everyday amenities. \n\nBushy Park itself is adjacent and provides extensive recreational facilities, including walking trails, tennis and padel courts. \n\nTempleogue Tennis Club is within walking distance, while Rathfarnham and Milltown Golf Clubs are only a short drive away. \n\nExcellent transport links including a conveniently located bus stop at the entrance to the development provides straightforward access to Dublin city centre while easy access to the M50, ensure ease of travel further afield.",
